      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1221494977,
      "text": "Syzygium corynanthum, commonly known as sour cherry and Killarney satinash, is a common Australian tree which grows in surrounding areas from Taree, New South Wales to tropical Queensland.The habitat of Syzygium corynanthum is rainforest on basaltic or fertile alluvial soils."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Syzygium corynanthum",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syzygium_corynanthum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 172064312,
      "text": "Syzygium corynanthum, es una especie de árbol perteneciente a la familia de las mirtáceas."
    }
